"hadiths[91]{hadithnumber,text}:"
3652,"Ibn 'Umar (Allah be pleased with them) reported that he divorced his wife while she was menstruating during the lifetime of Allah's Messenger (ﷺ). 'Umar b. Khattib (Allah be pleased with him) asked Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) about it"
3653,"Abdullah (b. 'Umar) reported that he divorced a wife of his with the pronouncement of one divorce during the period of menstruation. Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) commanded him to take her back and keep her until she was purified"
3654,"Ibn Umar (Allah be pleased with them) reported:I divorced my wife during the lifetime of Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) when she was in the state of menses. 'Umar (Allah be pleased with him) made a mention of it to Allah's Messenger (ﷺ)"
3655,"A hadith like this has been narrated on the authority of 'Ubaidullah"
3656,"Ibn 'Umar (Allah be pleased with them) reported that he divorced his wife during the period of menses. 'Umar (Allah be"
3657,"Abdullah b. 'Umar (Allah be pleased with them) reported:I divorced my wife while she was in the state of menses. 'Umar (Allah be pleased with him) made mention of it to Allah's Apostle (ﷺ) and he was enraged and he said: Command him to take her back until she enters the second ensuing menses other than the one in which he divorced her and in case he deems proper to divorce her"
3658,"A hadith like this was reported on the authority of Zuhri with the same chain of narrators. Ibn Umar (Allah be pleased with them)"
3659,"Ibn 'Umar (Allah be pleased with them) reported that he divorced his wife while she was in the state of menses. 'Umar (Allah be pleased with him) made mention of it to Allah's Apostle (ﷺ) and he said:Command him to take her back"
3660,"Ibn 'Umar (Allah be pleased with them) reported that he divorced his wife while she was in her menses. 'Umar (Allah be pleased with him) asked Allah's Apostle (ﷺ) about that"
3661,"Ibn Sirin reported:One who was blameless (as a narrator) narrated to me for twenty years that Ibn 'Umar (Allah be pleased with him) pronounced three divorces to his wife while she was in the state of menses. He was commanded to take her back. I neither blamed them (the narrators) nor recognised the hadith (to be perfectly genuine) until I met Abu Ghallab Yunus b. Jubair al-Bahili and he was very authentic"
3662,"A hadith like this has been transmitted on the authority of Ayyub with a slight variation of words"
3663,"Ayyub reported a hadith like this with the same chain of narrators and he said:Umar (Allah be pleased with him) asked Allah's Apostle (ﷺ) about it and he commanded him that he should take her back until she is divorced in the state of purity without having a sexual intercourse with her"
3664,"Yunus b. Jubair reported:I said to Ibn'Umar (Allah be pleased with them): A person divorcedhis wife while she was in the state of menses"
3665,"Ibn 'Umar (Allah be pleased with them) reported:I divorced my wife while she was in the state of menses. 'Umar (Allah he pleased wish him) came toAllah's Apostle (ﷺ) and made mention of that to him"
3666,"Anas b. Sirin reported:I asked Ibn 'Umar (Allah be pleased with them) about the woman whom he had divorced. He said: I divorced her while she was in the state of menses. It was mentioned to 'Umar (Allah be pleased with him) and he then made a mention of that to Allah's Apostle (ﷺ)"
3667,"Anas b. Sirin reported that he had heard Ibn 'Umar (Allah be pleased with them) as saying. I divorced my wife while she was in the state of menses. 'Umar (Allah be pleased with him) came to Allah's Apostle (ﷺ) and informed him about it"
3668,"This hadith has been narrated on the authority of Shu'ba with the same chain of transmitters but with a slight variation in wording"
3669,"Ibn Tawus narrated on the authority of his father that Ibn 'Umar (Allah be pleased with them) was asked about the person who divorced his wife in the state of menses"
3670,"Abu Zubair reported that he heard 'Abd al-Rahman b. Aiman (the freed slave of 'Azza) say that he asked Ibn 'Umar (Allah be pleased with them) and Abu Zubair heard:What is your opinion about the person who divorced his wife in the state of menses? Thereupon he said: Ibn Umar (Allah be pleased with them) divorced his wife during the lifetime of Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) while she was in the state of menses. Upon this Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) told him to take her back and so he took her back and he (further) said: When she is pure"
3671,"The story in the above hadith has likewise been narrated through another chain"
3672,"A hadith like this is reported on the same authority (but with this difference that the narrator) 'Abd al-Rahman b. Aiman (was mentioned) as the freed slave of 'Urwa (Imam Muslim said:He made a mistake who said that it was 'Urwa; it was in fact the freed slave of 'Azza)"
3673,"Ibn 'Abbas (Allah be pleased with them) reported that the (pronouncement) of three divorces during the lifetime of Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) and that of Abu Bakr and two years of the caliphate of Umar (Allah be pleased with him) (was treated) as one. But Umar b. Khattab (Allah be pleased with him) said:Verily the people have begun to hasten in the matter in which they are required to observe respite. So if we had imposed this upon them"
3674,"Abu Sahba' said toIbn 'Abbas (Allah be pleased with them):Do you know that three (divorces) were treated as one during the lifetime of Allah's Apostle (ﷺ)"
3675,"Abu al-Sahba' said to Ibn 'Abbas:Enlighten us with your information whether the three divorces (pronounced at one and the same time) were not treated as one during the lifetime of Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) and Abu Bakr. He said: It was in fact so"
3676,"Ibn Abbas (Allah be pleased with them) reported about (declaring of one's woman) unlawful as an oath which must be atoned"
3677,"Ibn Abbas (Allah be pleased with them) reported:When a man declares his wife unlawful for himself that is an oath which must be atoned"
3678,"A'isha (Allah be pleased with her) narrated that Allah's Apostle (ﷺ) used to spend time with Zainab daughter of Jahsh and drank honey at her house. She ('A'isha further) said:I and Hafsa agreed that one whom Allah's Apostle (ﷺ) would visit first should say: I notice that you have an odour of the Maghafir (gum of mimosa). He (the Holy Prophet) visited one of them and she said to him like this"
3679,"A'isha (Allah be pleased with her) reported Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) liked sweet (dish) and honey. After saying the afternoon prayer he used to visit his wives going close to them. So he went to Hafsa and stayed with her more than what was his usual stay. I ('A'isha) asked about that. It was said to me:A woman of her family had sent her a small vessel of honey as a gift"
3680,"This hadith has been narrated on the authority of 'Urwa with the same chain of transmitters"
3681,"A'isha (Allah be pleased with her) reported:When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was commanded to give option to his wives"
3682,"A'isha (Allah be pleased with her) reported that Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) sought our permission when he had a (turn to spend) a day with (one of his wives) amongst us (whereas he wanted to visit his other wives too). It was after this that this verse was revealed:"""" Thou mayest put off whom thou pleasest of them"
3683,"The above hadith has likewise been narrated through another chain"
3684,"A'isha reported:Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) gave us the option (to get divorce) but we did not deem it as divorce"
3685,"Masruq reported:I do not mind if I give option to my wife (to get divorce) once"
3686,"A'isha reported that Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) gave option to his wives"
3687,"A'isha (Allah be pleased with her) reported:Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) gave us the option (to get divorce) and we chose him and he did not count it a divorce"
3688,"A'isha (Allah be pleased with her) reported:Allah's Messeinger (ﷺ) gave us the option (to get divorce)"
3689,"A hadith like this has been transmitted on the authority of 'A'isha through another chain of narrators"
3690,"Jabir b. 'Abdullah (Allah be pleased with them) reported:Abu Bakr (Allah be pleased with him) came and sought permission to see Allah's Messenger (ﷺ). He found people sitting at his door and none amongst them had been granted permission"
3691,"Zuhair bin Harb told me, Umar bin Yunus al-Hanafi told us, Ikrimah bin Ammar told us, from Simak Abu Zumail, Abdullah bin Abbas told me, Umar bin al-Khattab told me, he said: ""When the Prophet of Allah (may Allah bless him and grant him peace) withdrew from his wives, I entered the mosque and found the people striking the ground with pebbles, saying: 'The Messenger of Allah (may Allah bless him and grant him peace) has divorced his wives.' That was before they were commanded to observe the veil (hijab). Umar said: I said, 'I shall certainly find out about this today.' He said: So I went in to Aishah and said, 'O daughter of Abu Bakr, has it come to this, that you would trouble the Messenger of Allah (may Allah bless him and grant him peace)?' She said, 'What business is it of mine and yours, O son of al-Khattab? Attend to your own affairs.' He said: So I went in to Hafsah bint Umar and said to her, 'O Hafsah, has it come to this, that you would trouble the Messenger of Allah (may Allah bless him and grant him peace)? By Allah, you know well that the Messenger of Allah (may Allah bless him and grant him peace) does not love you, and were it not for me, the Messenger of Allah (may Allah bless him and grant him peace) would have divorced you.' She wept most bitterly. I said to her, 'Where is the Messenger of Allah (may Allah bless him and grant him peace)?' She said, 'He is in his storeroom in the loft (mashrubah).' So I entered, and there I found Rabah, the servant of the Messenger of Allah (may Allah bless him and grant him peace), sitting on the threshold of the loft, with his legs dangling over a hollowed-out piece of wood, which was a trunk that the Messenger of Allah (may Allah bless him and grant him peace) would climb up and down on. I called out, 'O Rabah, ask permission for me to see the Messenger of Allah (may Allah bless him and grant him peace).' Rabah looked up at the room, then looked at me, and said nothing. Then I said, 'O Rabah, ask permission for me to see the Messenger of Allah (may Allah bless him and grant him peace).' Rabah looked up at the room, then looked at me, and said nothing. Then I raised my voice and said, 'O Rabah, ask permission for me to see the Messenger of Allah (may Allah bless him and grant him peace), for I think that the Messenger of Allah (may Allah bless him and grant him peace) thinks I have come because of Hafsah. By Allah, if the Messenger of Allah (may Allah bless him and grant him peace) ordered me to strike her neck, I would strike her neck.' I raised my voice, and he gestured to me to come up. So I went in to the Messenger of Allah (may Allah bless him and grant him peace), and he was lying on a mat. I sat down, and he drew his lower garment closer around himself - he had nothing else on - and the mat had left marks on his side. I looked around with my eyes at the storeroom of the Messenger of Allah (may Allah bless him and grant him peace), and there I found a handful of barley, about a sa' in quantity, and a similar amount of acacia leaves (used for tanning) in a corner of the room, and a hide hanging up. My eyes filled with tears. He said: 'What makes you weep, O son of al-Khattab?' I said, 'O Prophet of Allah, why should I not weep, when this mat has left marks on your side, and this is your storeroom in which I see only what I see, while that Caesar and that Khosrau live amid fruits and rivers, and you are the Messenger of Allah (may Allah bless him and grant him peace) and His chosen one, and this is your storeroom?' He said, 'O son of al-Khattab, are you not satisfied that we should have the Hereafter and they should have this world?' I said, 'Yes indeed.'"" He said: ""And I went in to him when I entered, and I could see anger in his face. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, why should the matter of the women distress you? If you have divorced them, then Allah is with you, and His angels, and Gabriel, and Michael, and I and Abu Bakr, and the believers are with you.' Rarely did I speak - and I praise Allah for it - a word, but I hoped that Allah would confirm the truth of what I said."" And this verse came down, the verse of choice (āyat al-takhyīr): ""Perhaps his Lord, if he divorced you, would substitute for him wives better than you"" [Surah at-Tahrim 66:5], and ""If you two (wives) cooperate against him, then indeed Allah is his protector, and Gabriel, and the righteous among the believers, and the angels are also his supporters"" [Surah at-Tahrim 66:4]. Aishah bint Abu Bakr and Hafsah used to cooperate against the rest of the wives of the Prophet (may Allah bless him and grant him peace). I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, have you divorced them?' He said, 'No.' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I entered the mosque, and the Muslims were striking the ground with pebbles, saying, ""The Messenger of Allah (may Allah bless him and grant him peace) has divorced his wives."" Shall I go down and tell them that you have not divorced them?' He said, 'Yes, if you wish.' So I kept talking to him until the anger left his face, until he smiled, and he had one of the most beautiful smiles among people. Then the Prophet of Allah (may Allah bless him and grant him peace) came down, and I came down. I came down clinging to the trunk, while the Messenger of Allah (may Allah bless him and grant him peace) came down as though he were walking on the ground, not touching it with his hand. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, you were in the loft for twenty-nine days.' He said, 'The month can be twenty-nine days.' I stood at the door of the mosque and called out at the top of my voice, 'The Messenger of Allah (may Allah bless him and grant him peace) has not divorced his wives.'"" And this verse came down: ""And when there comes to them information about [public] security or fear, they spread it around. But if they had referred it to the Messenger or to those in authority among them, those seeking to derive correct conclusions would have known about it [from them]"" [Surah an-Nisa 4:83]. And it was I who had derived that matter, and Allah, Exalted and Glorious, revealed the verse of choice."
3692,"Harun bin Sa'id Al-Aili narrated to us, Abdullah bin Wahb narrated to us, Sulaiman (meaning Ibn Bilal) informed me, Yahya informed me, Ubaid bin Hunain informed me that he heard Abdullah bin Abbas narrating: I remained for a year wanting to ask Umar bin Al-Khattab about a verse, but I could not ask him out of awe of him, until he went out for Hajj and I went out with him. When he returned, and we were on part of the road, he turned aside to the arak trees to relieve himself. I waited for him until he finished, then I walked with him, and I said: ""O Commander of the Believers, who are the two who conspired against the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) among his wives?"" He said: ""That was Hafsah and Aishah."" I said to him: ""By Allah, I had wanted to ask you about this for a year, but I could not out of awe of you."" He said: ""Do not do that. Whatever you think I have knowledge of, ask me about it, and if I know it I will tell you.""

He (Ibn Abbas) said: And Umar said: ""By Allah, during the time of ignorance (Jahiliyyah) we did not count women as having any importance, until Allah Most High revealed concerning them what He revealed, and allotted to them what He allotted."" He said: ""While I was engaged in a matter I was considering, my wife said to me: 'If only you would do such and such.' I said to her: 'What is it to you and what business is it of yours to interfere in a matter I intend to do?' She said to me: 'How strange you are, O son of Al-Khattab! You do not want to be answered back, yet your daughter answers back the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) until he remains angry for the whole day.'""

Umar said: ""So I took my cloak and went out at once until I entered upon Hafsah, and I said to her: 'O my daughter, do you answer back the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) until he remains angry for the whole day?' Hafsah said: 'By Allah, we do answer him back.' I said: 'Know that I warn you of the punishment of Allah and the anger of His Messenger. O my daughter, do not let this one deceive you who is pleased with her own beauty and the love the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) has for her' - meaning Aishah.""

""Then I went out until I entered upon Umm Salamah, because of my kinship with her, and I spoke to her. Umm Salamah said to me: 'How strange you are, O son of Al-Khattab! You have intruded into everything, until you now wish to intrude between the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) and his wives.' He said: She rebuked me so sharply that it took away some of what I was feeling, and I left her.""

""I had a companion from among the Ansar; when I was absent he would bring me news, and when he was absent I would bring him news. We were at that time fearful of a king among the kings of Ghassan, of whom it was mentioned to us that he intended to march against us, so our hearts were filled with concern about him. My companion from the Ansar came knocking at the door and said: 'Open, open!' I said: 'Has the Ghassani come?' He said: 'Something more serious than that - the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) has separated from his wives.' I said: 'May the nose of Hafsah and Aishah be rubbed in the dust!' Then I took my garment and went out until I came, and there was the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) in an upper chamber of his, which was reached by a ladder, and a black servant of the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) was at the top of the stairs. I said: 'This is Umar,' and I was given permission.""

Umar said: ""So I related to the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) this account, and when I reached the account of Umm Salamah, the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) smiled. He was lying on a mat with nothing between him and it, and under his head was a leather pillow stuffed with palm fibre, and at his feet was a pile of tanning bark, and at his head were hanging hides. I saw the mark of the mat on the side of the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him), and I wept.""

He said: ""What makes you weep?"" I said: ""O Messenger of Allah, Khosrau and Caesar live in such luxury, while you are the Messenger of Allah."" The Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) said: ""Are you not pleased that theirs should be this world and yours the Hereafter?"""
3693,"Ibn Abbas (Allah be pleased with them) said:I came along with Umar until we reached Marr al-Zahran (the name of a place)"
3694,"Ibn Abbas (Allah be pleased with them) is reported to have said:I intended to ask Umar about those two ladies who had pressed for (worldly riches) during the lifetime of the Prophet (ﷺ)"
3695,"Ishaq bin Ibrahim Al-Hanzali and Muhammad bin Abi 'Umar narrated this hadith to us with very similar wording. Ibn Abi 'Umar said: ""Abdur-Razzaq narrated to us,"" while Ishaq said: ""Abdur-Razzaq informed us""; he said: Ma'mar informed us, from Az-Zuhri, from 'Ubaidullah bin 'Abdullah bin Abi Thawr, from Ibn 'Abbas who said:

I had long wished to ask 'Umar about the two women among the wives of the Prophet (may peace be upon him) about whom Allah, the Exalted, said: ""If you two (wives) turn in repentance to Allah, your hearts are indeed so inclined"" (Surah At-Tahrim, 66:4), until 'Umar went for Hajj, and I went for Hajj with him. When we were on part of the road, 'Umar turned aside, and I turned aside with him carrying a water-vessel. He relieved himself, then came to me, and I poured water on his hands and he performed ablution. I said: ""O Commander of the Faithful, who were the two women among the wives of the Prophet (may peace be upon him) to whom Allah, Mighty and Sublime, said: 'If you two (wives) turn in repentance to Allah, your hearts are indeed so inclined'?"" 'Umar said: ""I am astonished at you, O Ibn 'Abbas."" (Az-Zuhri said: By Allah, he disliked what he had asked him about, but he did not conceal it from him.) He said: ""They are Hafsah and 'Aishah."" Then he began to relate the story. He said:

We, the tribe of Quraish, were a people who dominated our women, but when we came to Madinah, we found a people whose women dominated them, so our women began to learn from their women. My house was among the Banu Umayyah bin Zaid in the 'Awali (upper part of Madinah). One day I became angry with my wife, and she began to answer me back. I was displeased that she answered me back, and she said: ""Why are you displeased that I answer you back? By Allah, the wives of the Prophet (may peace be upon him) answer him back, and one of them may keep away from him for the whole day until night."" This alarmed me, so I went and entered upon Hafsah and said: ""Do you answer back the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him)?"" She said: ""Yes."" I said: ""Does one of you keep away from him for a whole day until night?"" She said: ""Yes."" I said: ""Whoever among you does that has certainly failed and lost. Does any of you feel secure that Allah will not become angry with her because of the anger of His Messenger (may peace be upon him), and then she would be ruined? Do not answer back the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him), nor ask him for anything, but ask me for whatever you need. And do not let it deceive you that your co-wife is more beautiful and more beloved to the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) than you"" - meaning 'Aishah.

He said: I had a neighbor from among the Ansar, and we used to take turns going down to the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him); he would go down one day and I would go down another day. He would bring me news of revelation and other matters, and I would bring him the same. We used to talk about how the Ghassan were shoeing their horses to attack us. My companion went down (to the Prophet), then came to me in the evening and knocked on my door and called me. I went out to him, and he said: ""A great matter has happened."" I said: ""What is it? Has Ghassan come?"" He said: ""No, it is greater and more serious than that: the Prophet (may peace be upon him) has divorced his wives."" I said: ""Hafsah has failed and lost. I had thought this would happen."" When I had prayed the dawn prayer, I put on my clothes, then went down and entered upon Hafsah, and she was weeping. I said: ""Has the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) divorced you all?"" She said: ""I do not know. He is there, secluded in this upper room."" I went to a black slave-boy of his and said: ""Seek permission for 'Umar."" He went in, then came out to me and said: ""I mentioned you to him, but he remained silent."" So I went and reached the pulpit and sat down. There was a group sitting near it, some of them weeping. I sat for a while, then what I was feeling overwhelmed me, and I went again to the slave-boy and said: ""Seek permission for 'Umar."" He went in, then came out to me and said: ""I mentioned you to him, but he remained silent."" So I turned to leave, and then the slave-boy called me and said: ""Enter, for he has given you permission."" I entered and greeted the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him), and found him reclining on a mat of palm-fiber which had left marks on his side. I said: ""Have you divorced your wives, O Messenger of Allah?"" He raised his head to me and said: ""No."" I said: ""Allah is Greater! If you had seen us, O Messenger of Allah - we, the tribe of Quraish, were a people who dominated our women, but when we came to Madinah, we found a people whose women dominated them, so our women began to learn from their women. I became angry with my wife one day, and she began to answer me back, and I was displeased that she answered me back. She said: 'Why are you displeased that I answer you back? By Allah, the wives of the Prophet (may peace be upon him) answer him back, and one of them may keep away from him for the whole day until night.' I said: 'Whoever among them does that has certainly failed and lost. Does any of them feel secure that Allah will not become angry with her because of the anger of His Messenger (may peace be upon him), and then she would be ruined?'"" The Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) smiled. I said: ""O Messenger of Allah, I entered upon Hafsah and said: 'Do not let it deceive you that your co-wife is more beautiful than you and more beloved to the Messenger of Allah (may peace be upon him) than you.'"" He smiled again. I said: ""May I sit with you comfortably, O Messenger of Allah?"" He said: ""Yes."" So I sat down, and I raised my head in the room, and by Allah, I saw nothing in it that caught the eye except three hides. I said: ""O Messenger of Allah, pray to Allah to grant abundance to your Ummah, for He has granted abundance to the Persians and the Romans, though they do not worship Allah."" He sat up straight and said: ""Are you in doubt, O son of Al-Khattab? Those are a people to whom their good things have been given in advance in the life of this world."" I said: ""Ask forgiveness for me, O Messenger of Allah."" He had sworn not to enter upon them for a month, due to the intensity of his displeasure with them, until Allah, Mighty and Sublime, rebuked him (for this oath)."
3696,"Ibn 'Abbas (Allah be pleased with them) reported. I had always been anxious to ask 'Umar (Allah be pleased with him) about the two ladies amongst the wives of Allah's Prophet (may peace be upon Lim) about whom Allah"
3697,"Fatima bint Qais reported that Abu 'Amr b. Hafs divorced her absolutely when he was away from home"
3698,"Fatima bint Qais reported that her husband divorced her during the life time of Allah's Prophet (ﷺ) and gave her a meagre maintenance allowance. When she saw that"
3699,"Fatima bint Qais reported that her husband al-Makhzulmi divorced her and refused to pay her maintenance allowance. So she came to Allah's Messenger (may peace he upon him) and informed him"
3700,"Abu Salama reported that Fatima bint Qais, the sister of al-Dahhak b. Qais informed him that Abu Hafs b. Mughira al-Makhzumi divorced her three times and then he proceeded on to the Yemen. The members of his family said to her:
There is no maintenance allowance due to you from us. Khalid b. Walid along with a group of persons visited Allah's Messenger ( صلی اللہ علیہ وسلم ) in the house of Maimuna and they said: Abu Hafs has divorced his wife with three pronouncements; is there any maintenance allowance due to her? Thereupon Allah's Messenger ( صلی اللہ علیہ وسلم ) said: No maintenance allowance is due to her, but she is required to spend the 'Idda; and he sent her the message that she should not be hasty in making a decision about herself and commanded her to move to the house of Umm Sharik, and then sent her the message that as the first immigrants (frequently) visit the house of Umm Sharik, she should better go to the house of Ibn Umm Maktum, the blind, (and further said: In case you put off your head-dress, he (Ibn Umm Makhtum) will not see you. So she went to his house, and when the 'Idda was over, Allah's Messenger ( صلی اللہ علیہ"
3701,"Fatima bint Qais reported:I had been married to a person from Banu Makhzum and he divorced me with irrevocable divorce. I sent a message to his family asking for maintenance allowance"
3702,"Fatima bint Qais (Allah be pleased with her) reported that she had been married to Abu 'Amr b. Hafs b. al-Mughira and he divorced her with three pronouncements. She stated that she went to Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) asking him about abandoning that house. He commanded her to move to the house of Ibn Umm Maktum"
3703,"This hadith has been transmitted through another chain of narrators"
3704,"Ubaidullah b. 'Abdullah b. 'Utba reported that 'Amr b. Hafs b. al-Mughira set out along with 'Ali b. Abi Talib (Allah be pleased with him) to the Yemen and sent to his wife the one pronouncement of divorce which was still left from the (irrevocable) divorce; and he commanded al-Harith b. Hisham and 'Ayyash b. Abu Rabi'a to give her maintenance allowance. They said to her:By Allah"
3705,"Sha'bi reported:I visited Fatima bint Qais and asked her about the verdict of Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) about (board and lodging during the 'Idda) and she said that her husband divorced her with an irrevocable divorce. She (further. said): I contended with him before Allah's Messerger (ﷺ) about lodging and maintenance allowance"
3706,"A hadith like this has been trarismitted on the authority of Hushaim through another chain of narrators"
3707,"Sha'bi reported:We visited Fatima bint Qais and she served us fresh dates and a drink of barley flour"
3708,"Fatima bint Qais (Allah be pleased with her) reported from Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) that there is no lodging and maintenance allowance for a woman who has been given irrevocable divorce"
3709,"Fatima bint Qais (Allah be pleased with her) reported:My husband divorced me with three pronouncements. I decided to move (from his house to another place). So I came to Allah's Messenger (ﷺ)"
3710,"Abu Ishaq reported:I was with al-Aswad b. Yazid sitting in the great mosque"
3711,"A hadith like this has been narrated on the authority of Ishaq with the same chain of transmitters"
3712,"Fatima bint Qais (Allah be pleased with her) reported that her husband divorced her with three"
3713,"Fatima bint Qais (Allah be pleased with her) reported:My husband Abu 'Amr b. Hafs b. al-Mughira sent 'Ayyish b. Abu Rabi'a to me with a divorce"
3714,"Abu Bakr b. Abu'l-Jahm reported:I and Abu Salama b 'Abd al-Rahman came to fatima bint Qais (Al! ah be pleased with her) and asked her (about divorce"
3715,"Abu Bakr reported:I and Abu Salama came to Fatima bint Qais (Allah be pleased with her) during the time of Ibn Zubair (Allah be pleased with him) and she narrated to us that her husband gave her an irrevocable divorce. (The rest of the hadith is the same)"
3716,"Fatima bint Qais (Allah be pleased with her) reported:My husband divorced me with three pronouncements and Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) made no provision for lodging and maintenance allowance"
3717,"Hisham reported on the authority of his father that Yahya b. Sa'id b. al-'As married the daughter of 'Abd al-Rahman b. al-Hakam"
3718,"Fatima bint Qais (Allah be pleased with her) reported that she said:Allah's Messenger"
3719,"A'isha (Allah be pleased with her) said:It is no good for Fatima to make mention of it"
3720,"Ibn al-Qasim narrated on the authority of his father that 'Urwa b. Zubair (Allah be pleased with him) said to 'A'isha (Allah be pleased with her):Didn't you see that such and such daughter of al-Hakam was divorced by her husband with an irrevocable divorce"
3721,"Jabir b. 'Abdullah (Allah be pleased with them) reported:My maternal aunt was divorced"
3722,"Ubaidullah b. 'Abdullah b. 'Utba (b. Mas'ud) reported that his father wrote to Umar b. 'Abdullah b al Arqam al-Zuhri that he would go to Subai'ah bint al-Hirith al-Aslamiyya (Allah be pleased with her) and ask her about a verdict from him which Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) gave her when she had asked that from him (in regard to the termination of 'Idda at the birth of a child) 'Umar b. Abdullah wrote to 'Abdullah b. 'Utba informing him that Subai'ah had told him that she had been married to Sa'd b. Khaula and he belonged to the tribe of Amir b. Lu'ayy"
3723,"Abu Salama b. 'Abd al-Rahman and Ibn 'Abbas. (Allah be pleased with them) got together in the house of Abu Huraira (Allah be pleased with him) and began to discuss about the woman who gave birth to a child a few nights after the death of her husband. Ibn 'Abbas (Allah be pleased with then) ) said:Her 'Idda is that period which is longer of the two (between four months and ten days and the birth of the child"
3724,"This hadith has been narated with the same chain of transrmitters except with a small change of words (and that is):They sent him to Umm Salama"
3725,"Zainab (bint Abu Salama) (Allah be pleased with her) reported:I went to Umm Habiba"
3726,"Zainab (bint Abu Salama) (Allah be pleased with her) reported:I went to Umm Habiba"
3727,"Zainab (bint Abu Salama) (Allah be pleased with her) reported:I went to Umm Habiba"
3728,"Zainab (bint Abu Salama) (Allah be pleased with her) reported:I went to Umm Habiba"
3729,"Zainab bint Umm Salama (Allah be pleased with her) reported that a relative of Umm Habiba (Allah he pleased with her) died. She sent for a yellow (perfume) and applied that to her forearm and said:I"
3730,"This hadith was narrated by Zainab from her mother and from Zainab"
3731,"This hadith was narrated by Zainab from her mother and from Zainab"
3732,"Zainab bint Umm Salama (Allah be pleased with her) reported on the authority of her mother that a woman lost her husband. (As her eyes were ailing) they (her kith and kin) entertained fear about her eyes"
3733,"Humaid b. Nafi' narrated two traditions from Umm Salama dealing with collyrium and the other hadith from the wives of Allah's Prophet (ﷺ) except with this that no mention was made of Zainab"
3734,"Zainab bint Abu Salama reported that when the news of the death of Abu Safyan came to Umm Habiba she sent for yellow (perfume) on the third day and rubbed it on her forearms and on her cheeks and said:I had in fact no need of it"
3735,"Safiyya bint Abu 'Ubaid reported on the authority of Hafsa or 'A'isha (Allah be pleased with thein) or from both of them that Allah's Messenger (may peace he upon him) said:It is not permissible for a woman believing in Allah and the Hereafter (or believing in Allah and His Messenger) that she should observe mourning for the dead beyond three days except in case of her husband"
3736,"A hadith like this is transmitted on the authority of Nafi"
3737,"Safiyya bint Abu 'Ubaid reported that she heard Hafsa daughter of Umar (Allah be pleased with them)"
3738,"Safiyya bint Abu 'Ubaid narrated this tradition of Allah's Prophet (ﷺ) on the authority of some wives of Allah's Apostle (ﷺ)"
3739,"A'isha (Allah be pleased with her) reported Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) as saying:It is not permissible for a woman believing in Allah and the Hereafter to observe mourning on the dead for more than three (days)"
3740,"Umm `Atiyya (Allah be pleased with her) reported that Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) had said:A woman must not observe mourning for one who had died for more than three (days) except for four months and ten days in the case of her husband. And she must not wear a dyed garment except one of the types made of dyed yarn"
3741,"A hadith like this has been narrated on the authority of Hisham with the same chain of narrators but with a slight variation of words"
3742,"Umm 'Atiyya ('Allah be pleased with her) said:We were forbidden to observe mourning for the dead beyond three days except in the case of husband (where it is permissible) for four months and ten days"
